Observable mixin</p>\n","kind":"member","name":"observable","type":{"names":["Boolean"]},"defaultvalue":true,"scope":"static","longname":"observable","$longname":"observable","$kind":"property","id":9456,"neoClassName":"Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps"},{"comment":"/**\n         * @member {String} className='Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps'\n         * @protected\n         */","meta":{"filename":"GoogleMaps.mjs","lineno":31,"columnno":8,"path":"/Users/tobiasuhlig/.neo-ai/agents/neo-opus-grace/neomjs/pages/node_modules/neo.mjs/src/main/addon","code":{}},"kind":"member","name":"className","type":{"names":["String"]},"defaultvalue":"'Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps'","access":"protected","longname":"className","scope":"global","$longname":"className","$kind":"property","id":9457,"neoClassName":"Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps"},{"comment":"/**\n         * Remote calls arriving before `isReady` are cached instead of executed, which is what keeps\n         * them from touching `google` before `loadFiles()` has populated it.\n         *\n         * Only methods that dereference the `google` global on entry belong here. `create` and\n         * `geocode` both do (`new google.maps.Map`, `new google.maps.Geocoder`). `addMarker` also\n         * names `google.maps.Marker`, but reaches it only after its own `mapCreated` listener has\n         * fired, so it already waits; the rest operate on `me.maps[mapId]`, which cannot exist before\n         * `create` has run.\n         *\n         * `Neo.main.addon.OpenStreetMaps` declares `['create']` for the same reason — its `geocode`\n         * is an unimplemented stub, so it is silent on that method rather than excluding it.\n         * @member {String[]} interceptRemotes\n         * @protected\n         */","meta":{"filename":"GoogleMaps.mjs","lineno":47,"columnno":8,"path":"/Users/tobiasuhlig/.neo-ai/agents/neo-opus-grace/neomjs/pages/node_modules/neo.mjs/src/main/addon","code":{}},"description":"<p>Remote calls arriving before <code>isReady</code> are cached instead of executed, which is what keeps\nthem from touching <code>google</code> before <code>loadFiles()</code> has populated it.</p>\n<p>Only methods that dereference the <code>google</code> global on entry belong here. <code>create</code> and\n<code>geocode</code> both do (<code>new google.maps.Map</code>, <code>new google.maps.Geocoder</code>). <code>addMarker</code> also\nnames <code>google.maps.Marker</code>, but reaches it only after its own <code>mapCreated</code> listener has\nfired, so it already waits; the rest operate on <code>me.maps[mapId]</code>, which cannot exist before\n<code>create</code> has run.</p>\n<p><code>Neo.main.addon.OpenStreetMaps</code> declares <code>[&#39;create&#39;]</code> for the same reason — its <code>geocode</code>\nis an unimplemented stub, so it is silent on that method rather than excluding it.</p>\n","kind":"member","name":"interceptRemotes","type":{"names":["Array.<String>"]},"access":"protected","longname":"interceptRemotes","scope":"global","$longname":"interceptRemotes","$kind":"property","id":9458,"neoClassName":"Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps"},{"comment":"/**\n         * @member {Object} remote\n         * @protected\n         */","meta":{"filename":"GoogleMaps.mjs","lineno":52,"columnno":8,"path":"/Users/tobiasuhlig/.neo-ai/agents/neo-opus-grace/neomjs/pages/node_modules/neo.mjs/src/main/addon","code":{}},"kind":"member","name":"remote","type":{"names":["Object"]},"access":"protected","longname":"remote","scope":"global","$longname":"remote","$kind":"property","id":9459,"neoClassName":"Neo.main.addon.GoogleMaps"},{"comment":"/**\n     * @member {google.maps.Geocoder|null} maps=null\n     */","meta":{"filename":"GoogleMaps.mjs","lineno":72,"columnno":4,"path":"/Users/tobiasuhlig/.neo-ai/agents/neo-opus-grace/neomjs/pages/node_modules/neo.mjs/src/main/addon","code":{}},"kind":"member","name":"maps","type":{"names":["google.maps.Geocoder","null"]},"defaultvalue":null,"longname":"maps","scope":"global","$longname":"maps